; The bidder's first lead. Winning 42 pp. 9-10 (S-0022-b, S-0022-c), pp. 23-24
; (S-0038-b, S-0040-c), pp. 91-94 (S-0121-d, S-0125-c), pp. 183-184 (S-0232-b,
; S-0232-c, S-0232-d, S-0233-a, S-0233-d, S-0233-e); played in Hands 12, 14,
; 16, 17, 18, 23, 27, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34 and 35 (S-0042-c and S-0043-a,
; S-0045-a, S-0050-c, S-0084-b, S-0086-a, S-0105-a, S-0125-c, S-0133-a,
; S-0135-b: Hand 30's 6-5, a trump that is not count, missing the top,
; S-0138-b, S-0142-d, S-0144-a, S-0146-b, S-0150-b).
; Rule, in our words: lead trumps first, holding the top ones in sequence any
; of them (Hand 28 leads the 6-0 holding the 0-0), missing the top any trump.
; Exceptions, in the book's order of argument:
; - with two trumps, lead first the off that calls for no count and whose own
;   double you lack (Hand 27: the 6-2, whose ten is your own trump);
; - with four trumps, the top and the third but not the second, lead the top:
;   an opponent can double up on the second only 33/95 of the time;
; - with the top but not the second (and, holding four, not the third either),
;   lead a low trump and budget the trick: not the top, and not your trump
;   count tile, since that must not be the lead that loses (Hands 16, 29);
;   holding four, you may lead the top first when a trump count tile is out;
;   without the top, likewise any trump but the count: a lead that can lose
;   must not be the one that loses the count (Hand 30 leads the 6-5, keeping
;   the 6-4; S-0050-c's reason), unless every trump he holds is count;
; - with one off and four trumps or more, the off may go first; a permission,
;   not an instruction, and never in a bid of marks, where the off goes last.
;   The book's hands of that shape (12, 14 and 32) lead trump, so the policy
;   leads trump there and the permission stays in this header: no rule allows
;   the off (2026-10-14, #146; before, a rule allowed it, and where the bidder
;   held no sure trump it allowed the off alone). The permission's own
;   condition, and a repair that reads it, are repaired/one-off-lead-trump.silas.
; Replaces gates/c10-off-on-trick-one.silas,
; gates/c12a-four-trumps-lead-the-double.silas and
; gates/c12b-four-trumps-lead-low.silas. How it differs: C10 makes the off the
; only tile (against the book in Hands 12, 14, 17, 18, 23 and 32); C12B takes
; four trumps only and the lowest trump (the book's examples hold three, and
; Hand 23 leads the 1-1, not the 0-0), without the count exception; C12A and
; C12B are silent outside their shapes, where the book still leads trump (Hand
; 35's 4-4, S-0150-b). C12A is the book's rule; its Hand 34 lead is the
; book's, and double-dummy it sets a made 84 (S-0146-b): a question for the
; bidder's information, not for the encoding.
; The book does not rank the sure trumps: it says any of them, and its hands
; lead the double but for Hand 28's bait (GAPS.md, the book's silences). The
; policy allows them all.
; The book contradicts itself on the 6-5: p. 132 (S-0167-b) says the bidder
; most often leads a 6-5 off first, while in Hand 31 (S-0138-b), holding the
; 6-5 off, it leads the 2-2. This file encodes the worked hand: trump first.

(include book)

(policy first-lead
  (rule two-trumps-lead-the-straight-off (play off)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (trick-number 1)
    (next-actor b)
    (exactly-two-trumps)
    (own-legal off)
    (bare-off off)
    (not (calls-for-count off)))
  (rule double-up-lead-the-double (play top)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (trick-number 1)
    (next-actor b)
    (exactly-four-trumps)
    (top-trump top)
    (next-trump top second)
    (next-trump second third)
    (own-legal top)
    (not (own-legal second))
    (own-legal third))
  (rule double-up-lead-low (play lead)
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (trick-number 1)
      (next-actor b)
      (exactly-four-trumps)
      (some (roles top second third)
        (top-trump top)
        (next-trump top second)
        (next-trump second third)
        (own-legal top)
        (not (own-legal second))
        (not (own-legal third))
        (not (tile lead top)))
      (own-legal lead)
      (trump-tile lead)
      (count lead 0))
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (trick-number 1)
      (next-actor b)
      (exactly-three-trumps)
      (some (roles top second)
        (top-trump top)
        (next-trump top second)
        (own-legal top)
        (not (own-legal second))
        (not (tile lead top)))
      (own-legal lead)
      (trump-tile lead)
      (count lead 0))
    (pattern
      (viewer b)
      (bidder b)
      (trick-number 1)
      (next-actor b)
      (exactly-four-trumps)
      (some (roles second third)
        (top-trump lead)
        (next-trump lead second)
        (next-trump second third)
        (not (own-legal second))
        (not (own-legal third)))
      (some (roles stake) (live stake) (not (mine stake)) (trump-tile stake) (count-tile stake))
      (own-legal lead)))
  (rule lead-the-top-trumps (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (trick-number 1)
    (next-actor b)
    (own-legal lead)
    (sure-trump lead))
  (rule lead-a-trump (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (trick-number 1)
    (next-actor b)
    (own-legal lead)
    (trump-tile lead)
    (count lead 0))
  (rule lead-a-count-trump (play lead)
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (trick-number 1)
    (next-actor b)
    (own-legal lead)
    (trump-tile lead)))
